# 6. Java Concepts Used

The project will demonstrate:

## Classes

The application uses multiple classes to separate responsibilities.

## Objects

Each individual task is represented as a `Task` object.

## Encapsulation

Task fields are private and accessed through methods.

## Constructors

The `Task` constructor initializes new task objects.

## Methods

Methods are used to define task and task management behavior.

## Collections

An `ArrayList` is used to store multiple tasks.

## Exception Handling

`try` and `catch` are used to handle invalid user input and file errors.

## File Handling

Java file I/O classes are used to save and load tasks.

## Control Flow

Loops and conditional statements control the application menu and task operations.

